{"title":"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex polygon with 1415 vertices and perimeter 2001. Prove that we can find 3 vertices of N which form a triangle of area smaller than 1.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The largest side has length at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/1/111fcc99e0ba06119608a3a8b67974b9867f7007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2001}{1415}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the sum of the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f8263a51c3e04cdf532afbfa6955aa2363850b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1414$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> sides is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944a8e6ba61874d6aa219c6c3cd51b2d5cf27917.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2001\\cdot1414}{1415}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" />. Divide these sides into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4cac61733f1edf8017c1087c2a6e566482c198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$707$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> pairs of adjacent sides, and there exist one pair of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9bd87816553cdd19b220f5b6b35e7eba511ebca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\le \\frac{2001\\cdot1414}{1415\\cdot707}=\\frac{2001\\cdot2}{1415}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"242\" height=\"38\" />. Blah blah blah... we know how to prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/8/298f71cd66367e8c7700c3a0893b480cb4928662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2001\\cdot2}{1415} &lt; 2\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" /> except why would a problem want you to do that.... no idea.\n</p><p>Well, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a41926464c1cf9165c570859b2487f6b1a7e92e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{ab} &lt; a+b (AM-GM) &lt; 2\\sqrt2 \\Rightarrow ab &lt; 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"345\" height=\"22\" /> and the area of the triangle with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> and the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> between them has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f19b8373701a98f7ef13e3591db992b2e08f8ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12ab\\sin C \\le \\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{2} &lt;\\frac12\\cdot2\\cdot1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"288\" height=\"38\" /> as desired.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/user/61542\">AwesomeToad</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO\" title=\"2001 JBMO\">2001 JBMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13_contests\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JBMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" title=\"JBMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\"> All JBMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017153810\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 95/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 839/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 43/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2349/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.868      1 Template:JBMO_box\n100.00%    9.868      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23676:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017153810 and revision id 186114. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}